# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  This git repository is rooted at the HOME directory, but its
#  only purpose is to publish the GitHub profile repo
#  (github.com/Thibautdqb/Thibautdqb).
#
#  Strategy: ignore the ENTIRE home directory by default, then
#  re-include ONLY the files that belong to the profile. This
#  makes an accidental `git add -A` safe — it can never stage
#  secrets such as .aws/, .ssh/, .bash_history, .claude.json,
#  .config/, credentials, tokens, etc.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore everything at the top level of the home directory.
/*

# 2) Re-include only the profile files.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/assets/
!/.github/
